### Streaming with Suspense:
```typescript
import { Suspense } from 'react';

export default function Dashboard() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Header />
      <Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton />}>
        <DataTable /> {/* Async Server Component */}
      </Suspense>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Caching Strategies

```typescript
// No caching (always fresh)
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';

// ISR - Revalidate every hour
export const revalidate = 3600;

// Cache fetch requests
fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
  next: { revalidate: 3600 }
});

// Tag-based revalidation
fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
  next: { tags: ['user-data'] }
});
```

## Code Generation Preferences

When generating Next.js code:
1. Use Server Components by default
2. Add 'use client' only when necessary
3. Implement proper loading and error states
4. Use Server Actions for mutations
5. Include proper TypeScript types
6. Optimize images with next/image
7. Implement proper caching strategies
8. Add metadata for SEO
9. Use Suspense for async operations
10. Follow the App Router file structure
